# Manual QA Gate

Purpose:
  Enforces human verification before L0 → L1 transition.
  Uses hash-referenced test cases for token-efficient operator feedback.

Owns: testing\MANUAL-QA-GATE.sdd

## Hash-Referenced Test Cases

Format:
  Each manual test case receives a unique short hash displayed as a paragraph before the test description.

Example:
  #a3f9 — User profile page loads Story component when navigating to profile.
  #b71c — Expired subscriber sees rejection message on 5th video access attempt.

## Operator Response Format

Response:
  Operator replies per hash only (token efficiency):
    #a3f9: OK
    #b71c: FAIL — rejection message missing, video only buffers

## L0 → L1 Transition Rule

Rule:
  - AI MUST NOT self-declare "L0 complete, advancing to L1".
  - Transition requires explicit operator confirmation for EVERY hash.
  - Generic "tested, works" confirmation is NOT accepted.
  - Each hash must receive its own explicit OK or FAIL response.
  - ONLY after all hashes have explicit OK/FAIL does L0 become a "product".
  - ONLY then does L1 advancement begin.

## Lifecycle

L0_Status: pending|in_progress|awaiting_verification|complete
L1_Status: pending|blocked|in_progress
Hashes: [list of {hash}: {status}]
Operator_Verified_At: <timestamp>

State: +
